      "content": "exactly!! and it's not just the time. i checked the city website and they say they're \"improving water pressure\", but they haven't even touched the actual pipes when they're working. it's like they're just using the water crew as a cover to get access to the ground under our homes. if they're installing sensors for vibrations, that would explain why they're so precise about where they dig. do you think there's any way to figure out what kind of frequency these things might use or how they'd transmit the data back to a central hub?",
